> The truth is simple- some of the food being sold today is making us sick, and fixing that goes far beyond politics. The energy in Harrisburg was electric as U.S. Department of Health and Human Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy, Jr. launched his Eat Real Food Campaign, which is part of the Make America Healthy Again initiative. The message was simple, empower people with information, tools and knowledge to take charge of their well-being and be the CEO of their own health. The crowd responded with enthusiasm-because this wasn't just talk about policy, it was a call to action. Today didn't just feel like a press conference- it felt like the start of a healthier future.

